  "description": "Block built in 2002, 'Whispering Pines' offers the perfect blend of durability, space and convenience for modern family living.  Located on the edge of Trim town, just off the Navan road and a few minutes walk to the local Porchfields Boyne River walk and the many historical heritage sites.\r\nThe property is bright and spacious and offers 4 double bedrooms, one on the ground floor and three upstairs with two ensuites.The rest of the accommodation includes a ground floor shower room, generous kitchen/dining room with wood burning stove, sitting room with open fireplace,utility room and main bathroom.\r\nOutside there is a detached block built garage with WC and wash hand basin.  The property is surrounded to the rear by open green fields and a hand-built natural stone wall bounds the property at the front.\r\nAn ideal opportunity awaits the discerning purchaser to secure a solid block built detached property in a great location in the Heritage, and Tidy Towns Award Winning town of Trim.\n\nEntrance Hall Hardwood front door with glazed side panels, solid ash/maple wood flooring, alarm key pad.\n\nSitting Room Wooden fire surround with brick insert and open fireplace, solid ash/maple wood flooring,, ceiling coving, dual aspect windows with large bay window to the front overlooking garden.\n\nKitchen/dining Range of wall and floor kitchen units with tiled over countertop, Beko undermount fridge, filtered drinking tap, dishwasher, built-in Electrolux double oven, Belling 4 x ring ceramic hob with extractor fan over, tiled floor, brick chimney breast with cast-iron wood burning stove in the Dining end, pine panelled ceiling and PVC french doors leading out to rear garden and paved patio area,\n\nUtility Room Tall walk-in storage unit, built-in hot press with insulated cylinder and immersion heater, tiled floor, worktop with sink unit. Hoover tumble dryer and Bosch washing machine, Baxi gas boiler, PVC door to rear garden and block built shed.\n\nShower 